  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: A gap on the seafloor, falling to a depth of 1500m and separating Challenger Plateau from Lord Howe Rise. References: Tectonic map of the Southwest Pacific, Cullen 1970; Bellona Bathymetry, Carter & Eade, 1979."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature forms a narrow break at the E extreme of Chatham Rise, approximately 400 km NE of Chatham Islands. The name first appeared on Oceanic Bathymetry Series (OBS) chart 'Chatham' in 1969.Minimum depth (m): 1750. Maximum depth (m): 2200. Total relief (m): 450."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature has an elongated shape. It is located between the continental slope of Ceará State and Ceará Plateau. Minimum depth (m): 1500. Maximum depth (m): 2330. Total relief (m): 830. Dimension: ~ 70 km x 20 km"@en ;
