<http://shaclshapes.org/noteLedgesShapeProperty> rdf:type <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#PropertyShape> ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: Feature description: A bench (c.45m) on the west side of White Island, 1.9km from the north end at Cape Spencer-Smith, in the Ross Archipelago. The bench comprises the northwestern-most moraine-covered volcanic outcrops on the island, upon which occur tuffaceous conglomerate block and shelf fragments of the Scallop Hill Formation. History/Origin/Meaning: Named by US-ACAN (1999) after Ian G. Speden, N.Z. Geological Survey, DSM who, accompanied by A.C. Beck, collected fossiliferous deposits here, Dec. 22, 1958."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: Feature description: Broad relatively flat elevated area west of, and above Pyramid Trough. History/Origin/Meaning: Named by VUWAE 4 1960-61 (Victoria University of Wellington Antarctic Expedition) in association with Mount Dromedary."@en ;
  <http://shaclshapes.org/confidence> 4E-1 ;
