<http://shaclshapes.org/noteProvincePhysicalShapeProperty> rdf:type <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#PropertyShape> ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This province consists of combination of numerous small basins, ridges and associated escarpments. Multi-channel seismic profiles show clear evidence of development of syn-rift basins, including tilted horizons. Furthermore, the eastern edge of the provin"@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: associated meeting, proposer and year of proposal: Associated meeting: SCUFN-16. Proposer: José Luis Frias Salazar, National Institute of Statistics and Geography (INEGI), Mexico; and Lisa Taylor, National Geophysical Data Center (NGDC), USA. Year of proposal: 2003."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: associated meeting, proposer and year of proposal: Associated meeting: SCUFN-28. Proposer: Japanese Committee on Undersea Feature Names (JCUFN). Year of proposal: 2015. "@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: associated meeting, proposer and year of proposal: Associated meeting: SCUFN-34. Proposer: Japanese Committee on Undersea Feature Names (JCUFN). History: 2020."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: Japanese survey vessel "Shoyo". Year of discovery: 2002. History: Named after Dr Kazuo Kobayashi, a renowned Japanese marine geophysicst who died in August 2013. His primaly area of interest was the Philippine Sea, including the Kyushu-Palau R"""@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: Japanese survey vessel "Takuyo". Year of discovery: 1985. History: Named from the world-famous Japanese film character, Godzilla, and the Oceanic Core Complexes (OCCs), or megamullions, which cover this area. OCCs are domal bathymetric highs characterized by axis-normal surface corrugations and exposures of serpentinized peridotite and gabbroic rocks which are interpreted as exhumed footwalls of low-angle detachment faults. They provide a valuable opportunity to directly study the architecture of oceanic lithosphere, together with the tectono-magmatic processes associated with its formation and evolution, at oceanic spreading centers."""@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: Korean research vessel "Haeyang 2000". Year of discovery: 1998. History: Named from the nearby province of Jeollado, Rep. of Korea."""@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: Named from the nearby Mexican State of Campeche."@en ;
