  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: British vessel HMS "Owen". Year of discovery: 1960. History: Named after Dr. Roger Revelle (1909-1991), an acknowledged leader of 20th century oceanography (and other fields). As the first chairman of the Scientific Committee on Oceanic Resear"""@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: First appeared as Farewell Rise on Oceanic Bathymetry Series (OBS) chart  'Cook' in 1991. Altered to Onetahua Rise to restore the original Maori name of the associated land feature, Farewell Spit. "Onetahua" means 'sand hills'. """@en ;
