  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature is the roughly flat region around Campbell Island / Motu Ihupuku that ranges from c 100 m to c 200 m depth. The name first appeared    on Oceanic Bathymetry Series (OBS) chart ¿Campbell¿ in 1967. Minimum depth (m): 130. Maximum depth (m): 200. Total relief (m): 70."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature, adjacent to the Bounty Islands, is located approximately 740 km E-SE of the SE coast of the South Island of New Zealand. The name first appeared on Island Bathymetry Series (IBS) chart 'Bounty Island' in 1969. Minimum depth (m): 130. Maximum depth (m): 200. Total relief (m): 70. Dimension/size: 60 km x 60 km (demarcated by the 200 m isobath)."@en ;
