  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: New Zealand research vessel "Taranui". Year of discovery: 1970. History: Named in association with Kahurangi Point, the closest geographic feature on the nearby New Zealand mainland. ‘Kahurangi’ means ‘precious’ in Maori language. """@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: Named from the nearby Hikunui Island, east of Coromandel Peninsula, North Island of New Zealand."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: Named in assocation with Rakaia River on the adjacent mainland of New Zealand's South Island. Rakaia is the Ngai Tahu dialectal form of 'rangaia', which refers to the practice of strong men standing in line to break the force of the water when crossing a river."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: "Niglik" is of Inuit origin and the feature is named after the nearby Niglik Block, a name chosen by the oil company doing research in the area."""@en ;
